@article{ WOS:001357317900001,
Author = {Vos, Thijs and Otjes, Simon and van Kalken, Lianne and Boogaard, Geerten},
Title = {Beyond coalition and opposition? The effect of councilwide agreements on
   legislative voting behaviour in Dutch municipalities},
Journal = {SWISS POLITICAL SCIENCE REVIEW},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {31},
Number = {2},
Pages = {307-330},
Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {A well-established finding in the field of legislative behaviour is that
   parliamentary voting behaviour is nearly always strongly structured by
   the coalition-opposition dynamic, even beyond the issues agreed on in
   the coalition agreement. Can parties break the mould of this
   coalition-opposition division? Several Dutch municipal councils work
   with a councilwide agreement (raadsakkoord) with the specific goal that
   there is no demarcated coalition and opposition. This could open the
   political process up for more issue-driven voting. We test whether
   council agreements change voting behaviour in the local council. By
   comparing voting in these municipalities before and after implementing
   councilwide agreements, we show that these agreements lower the extent
   to which voting is structured by the coalition-opposition division.
   Coalition parties are less likely to vote the same when a councilwide
   agreement is present. The strength of the coalition-opposition division
   depends upon the choices of political parties.
   Die Forschung zum legislativen Verhalten hat etabliert, dass das
   Abstimmungsverhalten im Parlament fast immer stark durch die Dynamik von
   Koalition und Opposition strukturiert ist, selbst \& uuml;ber die im
   Koalitionsvertrag vereinbarten Themen hinaus. K \& ouml;nnen Parteien
   diese Spaltung zwischen Koalition und Opposition durchbrechen? Mehrere
   niederl \& auml;ndische Gemeinder \& auml;te arbeiten mit einem
   Ratsabkommen (raadsakkoord) mit dem spezifischen Ziel, dass es keine
   abgegrenzte Koalition und Opposition gibt. Dies k \& ouml;nnte den
   politischen Prozess f \& uuml;r ein st \& auml;rker themenorientiertes
   Abstimmungsverhalten \& ouml;ffnen. Wir testen, ob Ratsabkommen das
   Abstimmungsverhalten im Gemeinderat ver \& auml;ndern. Durch den
   Vergleich des Abstimmungsverhaltens in diesen Gemeinden vor und nach der
   Einf \& uuml;hrung von Ratsabkommen zeigen wir, dass die Abkommen den
   Grad, zu dem der Gegensatz zwischen Koalition und Opposition das
   Abstimmungsverhalten strukturiert, verringern. Koalitionsparteien
   stimmen weniger oft einheitlich ab, wenn Parteien ein Ratsabkommen
   geschlossen haben. Die St \& auml;rke der Spaltung zwischen Koalition
   und Opposition h \& auml;ngt von den Entscheidungen der politischen
   Parteien ab.
   La recherche sur le comportement l \& eacute;gislatif montre que le vote
   parlementaire est. fortement structur \& eacute; par la dynamique
   coalition-opposition, aussi sur des questions qui ne sont pas r \&
   eacute;gl \& eacute;es dans l'accord de coalition. Les partis
   peuvent-ils briser cette division coalition-opposition? Plusieurs
   conseils municipaux n \& eacute;erlandais travaillent avec un accord du
   conseil (raadsakkoord) visant \& agrave; \& eacute;viter cette d \&
   eacute;limitation. Cela pourrait ouvrir le processus politique \&
   agrave; des votes qui sont structur \& eacute;s par les division th \&
   eacute;matiques. Nous testons si ces accords modifient le comportement
   de vote dans le conseil municipal. En comparant les votes dans ces
   municipalit \& eacute;s avant et apr \& egrave;s la mise en oe uvre des
   accords de conseil, nous montrons que ces accords r \& eacute;duisent le
   degr \& eacute; auquel le vote est. structur \& eacute; par la division
   coalition-opposition. Les partis de coalition sont moins susceptibles de
   voter de mani \& egrave;re uniforme lorsqu'un accord de conseil est. en
   place. La force de la division coalition-opposition d \& eacute;pend des
   choix des partis politiques.
   Una scoperta ben consolidata nel campo del comportamento legislativo \&
   egrave; che le votazioni in parlamento sono quasi sempre fortemente
   strutturate dalla dinamica coalizione-opposizione, anche oltre le
   questioni concordate nell'accordo di coalizione. I partiti possono
   rompere lo schema di questa divisione coalizione-opposizione? Diversi
   legislativi comunali nei Paesi Bassi lavorano con accordi di
   legislazione (raadsakkoord) con l'obiettivo specifico di non avere una
   coalizione e un'opposizione delineate. Questa prassi potrebbe aprire il
   processo politico a votazioni pi \& ugrave; orientate a temi specifici.
   In questo studio esaminiamo se tali accordi cambiano il comportamento di
   voto nei legislativi comunali. Confrontando le votazioni prima e dopo
   l'attuazione degli accordi legislativi, mostriamo che gli accordi
   riducono la misura in cui le votazioni sono strutturate dalla divisione
   coalizione-opposizione. I partiti di coalizione hanno meno probabilit \&
   agrave; di votare nello stesso modo quando \& egrave; presente un
   accordo legislativo. La forza della divisione coalizione-opposizione
   dipende dalle scelte dei partiti politici.},
